    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.negative_edge_cycle - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.negative_edge_cycle.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.negative_edge_cycle()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if the graph contains a cycle of negative total weight.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.negative_edge_cycle()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if the graph contains a cycle of negative total weight.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.negative_edge_cycle()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Check if the graph contains a cycle of negative total weight.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCheck if the graph contains a cycle of negative total weight.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L59414-L59503){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.negative_edge_cycle(weighted=None)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Negative edge cycle](../assets/graphs/negative-edge-cycle.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three currencies linked by exchange edges weighted with negative log-rates. Left: USD to EUR −0.10, EUR to GBP −0.15 and GBP to USD +0.20 add up to −0.05, a negative cycle (accent) that signals an arbitrage loop, so negative_edge_cycle() returns True. Right: with GBP to USD at +0.30 the loop totals +0.05, so no cycle is negative and the call returns False.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nShortest paths are only well defined when no cycle has negative total weight; otherwise\ngoing around the cycle again always makes a route cheaper. Negative weights appear with\ncosts that can be gains (currency exchange rates as negative log-rates, refunds,\nenergy recovery), and a negative cycle then signals an arbitrage or modelling error.\nThis method checks the whole graph, whatever node a cycle is reachable from.\n\nOn an undirected graph every edge can be traversed both ways, so a single negative edge\nalready forms a negative cycle (there and back).\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to use edge weights. If `None` (default), follows the graph's `weighted`\n    flag (an unweighted graph has no negative cycle).\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `True` if some cycle has negative total weight.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nBellman-Ford is run from all nodes at once (distance 0 everywhere, equivalent to a\nvirtual source joined to every node, as in NetworkX); if distances still improve after\n$V$ rounds, a negative cycle exists. It runs in $O(VE)$ time.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~find_negative_cycle`) \n\n:   The nodes of one negative cycle.\n\n[](`~bellman_ford_shortest_path`) \n\n:   Shortest paths with negative weights, if no cycle is negative.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThree currencies whose exchange rates, as negative log-rates, admit an arbitrage loop:\n\n::: {#c2251d52 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nfx = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"USD\", \"EUR\", -0.10), (\"EUR\", \"GBP\", -0.15), (\"GBP\", \"USD\", 0.20)],\n    directed=True,\n)\n\nfx.negative_edge_cycle()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\nTrue\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Checking a table of exchange rates\n\n`currency()` holds the exchange rates quoted between six currencies, each edge weighted by\nthe negative log of its rate. Its stale euro–pound quotes make an arbitrage loop, while\nwith `arbitrage=False` they are corrected:\n\n::: {#da19143a .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\n(\n    ec.currency().negative_edge_cycle(),\n    ec.currency(arbitrage=False).negative_edge_cycle(),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(True, False)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nNegative weights alone don't make a negative cycle. In the corrected rates, the 9 quotes\nwith a rate above 1 (highlighted) have negative weights, but every cycle loses more to the\nspreads along it than these gain:\n\n::: {#61cd4b78 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfx = ec.currency(arbitrage=False)\nedges = fx.get_edge_df()\ngains = edges.filter(edges[\"weight\"] < 0)[\"id\"].to_list()\n\nfx.plot(\n    highlight_edges=gains, label_by=\"label\",\n    curved_edges=True, seed=4,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15